---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="DuBose, M.D. — direct primary care" bookbar={true}>

  <!-- 1 · Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="h-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">Direct primary care &middot; [City], Texas</span>
          <h1>A doctor with time to actually figure it out with you.</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="h-photo">
          <div class="photo-frame">
            <div class="photo" style="aspect-ratio:4/5">
              <img src="/images/dr-dubose.jpg" alt="Dr. Logan DuBose" width="800" height="1000" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-body">
          <p class="sub">
            I&rsquo;m Logan DuBose, a primary care physician. My practice is
            small on purpose: unhurried visits, direct messaging, and one
            doctor who follows your whole picture.
          </p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
            <a class="quiet" href="/how-it-works">How it works &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pstrip">
        <div><b>$100 a month</b>one flat price, no per-visit charges</div>
        <div><b>Cancel anytime</b>no contract, no sign-up fee</div>
        <div><b>Keeps your insurance</b>works alongside it, never instead of it</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · Recognition -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">The situation</span>
          <h2>If your health has started to feel like too much</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Maybe it&rsquo;s several things at once — blood pressure creeping
            up, poor sleep, results nobody explained, medications
            you&rsquo;re not sure you still need. You may have seen good
            specialists, each one checking their part, with no one looking
            at the whole of it.
          </p>
          <p>
            Or maybe nothing is wrong yet, and you want a doctor who knows
            you before something is.
          </p>
          <p>
            The problem usually isn&rsquo;t a lack of healthcare. It&rsquo;s
            that nobody has time to think it through with you.
          </p>
          <p><a class="quiet" href="/help">What I can help with &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · What I do -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">What I do</span>
          <h2>Primary care with enough time</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            I listen, understand your whole situation, sort out what&rsquo;s
            urgent and what can wait, and work a plan with you over time.
            Visits last as long as they need to. Between visits you can
            message me, and every result comes with my explanation.
          </p>
          <p>
            This is not alternative medicine or a wellness program. It is
            evidence-based primary care with enough time to do it well.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · How it works -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Membership</span>
        <h2>How it works</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step-item">
          <span class="num">01</span>
          <h4>We talk first</h4>
          <p>A free 30-minute video call. If I&rsquo;m not the right fit,
          I&rsquo;ll say so.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <span class="num">02</span>
          <h4>You join if it fits</h4>
          <p>$100 a month. No sign-up fee, no contract. Cancel anytime.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <span class="num">03</span>
          <h4>Care that fits you</h4>
          <p>Mostly by video. Home visits when an exam needs it; clinic
          space when that&rsquo;s better.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step-item">
          <span class="num">04</span>
          <h4>You see it working</h4>
          <p>Your blood pressure, labs, and progress are visible to both
          of us.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:36px"><a class="quiet" href="/how-it-works">The details, start to finish &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · The price -->
  <section class="section band-tint" id="bookbar-after">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Pricing</span>
        <h2>The price</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split even" style="align-items:start">
        <div class="price-card">
          <div class="amt">$100 <span>/ month per adult</span></div>
          <div class="per">no per-visit charges</div>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>Visits as your care needs them</li>
            <li>Direct messaging with me</li>
            <li>Every result explained</li>
            <li>Your care coordinated</li>
            <li>Forms and paperwork included</li>
            <li>Home visits when needed</li>
            <li>Cancel anytime</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <h3>What it doesn&rsquo;t cover</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:8px">
            Labs, imaging, medications, vaccines, specialists, hospitals.
            Your insurance keeps covering those, as it does today.
          </p>
          <h3 style="margin-top:28px">Medicare or Medicaid</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:8px">
            You can still join. One extra form, required by federal or
            state rules, handles it.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:24px"><a class="quiet" href="/pricing">Pricing &amp; how insurance fits &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · Honest fit -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Honest fit</span>
        <h2>Who this is for — and who it isn&rsquo;t</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="fit">
        <div>
          <h3>A good fit if&hellip;</h3>
          <ul class="yes">
            <li>you want a doctor who knows you</li>
            <li>your health feels tangled and you want help sorting it out</li>
            <li>you have ongoing conditions and want them managed, not just
            refilled</li>
            <li>you&rsquo;d rather prevent problems than chase them</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Not a fit if&hellip;</h3>
          <ul class="no">
            <li>you need 24/7 physician access — I keep business hours and
            take real time off</li>
            <li>you need emergency or hospital care — that is the
            ER&rsquo;s job, always</li>
            <li>you&rsquo;re under 18 — I care for adults only</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="soft" style="margin-top:28px">I&rsquo;d rather be clear about this now than disappoint you later.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7 · The doctor -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">The doctor</span>
          <h2>Logan DuBose, M.D.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            I&rsquo;m a physician and researcher. I built this practice
            because I kept meeting patients who didn&rsquo;t need more
            healthcare — they needed one doctor with enough time to think.
          </p>
          <p><a class="quiet" href="/about">More about me and how I practice &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 8 · Common questions -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
          <h2>Common questions</h2>
          <p style="margin-top:18px"><a class="quiet" href="/questions">All questions, answered &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>Is this health insurance?</summary>
          <p class="a">
            No. It is a direct agreement between you and me for my services
            as your physician. It does not replace insurance. I recommend
            every member keep coverage for everything outside our
            relationship — labs, medications, specialists, hospitals.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Why is it only $100 when concierge doctors charge thousands?</summary>
          <p class="a">
            The practice is small by design: no office building, no billing
            department, no staff, and a limited number of patients.
            Concierge fees typically run $2,400 to $5,000 a year on top of
            insurance billing. This is $100 a month, and I bill no one.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>I already have doctors I like — does this still make sense?</summary>
          <p class="a">
            Often, yes. You can keep every doctor you have, including
            another primary care physician. Members in that situation use
            me as the doctor who has time: to explain, to coordinate, and
            to watch the whole picture.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What&rsquo;s the catch?</summary>
          <p class="a">
            The limits are stated, not hidden: I keep business hours, I am
            not an emergency service, I take real time away each year, and
            when my panel is full it is full.
          </p>
        </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 9 · Closing invitation -->
  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>Start with a free conversation.</h2>
        <p>
          Thirty minutes by video. Tell me what&rsquo;s going on, and
          I&rsquo;ll tell you honestly whether I can help. If I&rsquo;m not
          the right fit, I&rsquo;ll point you toward someone good.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
        <div class="signup">
          <p>
            Not ready to talk? Leave your email and I&rsquo;ll send an
            occasional letter about the practice — no more than monthly.
          </p>
          <form action="#" method="post">
            <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="email address" aria-label="Email address" required />
            <button class="btn btn-inverse" type="submit">Send me the letter</button>
          </form>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
